close_reason: Implementation and sandboxed regression evidence complete; awaiting reviewed PR delivery.
body: "Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1462\n\n## Problem\nExtension packages render through the host, so TOON is their default output, and their acceptance tests need to assert on what the host actually printed. The public SDK (`@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk`, `/sdk/testing`, `/sdk/core`, …) exposes no TOON decoder: there is no `decodeToon`, `parseToon` or equivalent. Authors fall back to one of three bad options:\n1. **Hard-coding quoting**, as in `assert.match(out, /status: \"open\"/)`. This broke when the host renderer started emitting unquoted scalars (unbraind/pm-github#115 CI went red after a toolchain bump).\n2. **Deep-importing internals**: `import { decodeToonItemContent } from \"@unbrained/pm-cli/dist/core/item/toon-decode.js\"`. This sits outside the exports map and can break on any release.\n3. **Adding `@toon-format/toon` as a devDependency pinned to whatever pm-cli uses internally (4.1.1 today).** That duplicates the pin, and any skew means the test parser disagrees with the host renderer.\n\n## Proposal\n- Export `decodeToon(text)` (and ideally `encodeToon(value)`) from `@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/testing`, or from `/sdk`, backed by exactly the TOON implementation the host renders with.\n- In the authoring docs, recommend asserting host output as `decodeToon(stdout)` rather than by string matching.\n- Optional: `createExtensionTestHarness` gives a `run(...)` result exposing `.parsed` for both `--json` and TOON output.\n\nThat makes extension tests independent of quoting and whitespace changes in the renderer, and removes a reason to reach into `dist/`.\n\n\nImplementation intent\n\nExpose a typed public SDK testing codec over the same pinned TOON implementation used by the host renderer, enabling semantic output assertions without deep imports or duplicated package dependencies."
